From 008ac8dd271c06deb35b44993dec1a9c757626e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:58:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 31/97] graphics: on-demand GPU->CPU visibility for resolved
 data

CommandProcessor::MakeGpuWritesVisibleToCpu(guest_address, length) copies back, synchronously
and only when asked, the pages of a range whose current data exists only on the GPU (the shared
memory's valid-and-GPU-written page bits), so newer CPU writes are never overwritten. Callable
from any thread: a mutex/condition-variable request slot is serviced by the worker thread
between command batches and while idle (pending_fns_ is not thread-safe), with a timeout so a
worker blocked on the caller cannot deadlock. Vulkan implements it with a transfer from the
shared memory buffer; draw-resolution scaling is not handled (returns false).

For titles whose CPU code reads render-to-texture results. readback_resolve=full makes WWE '13's
composited wrestler textures correct but halves its in-ring frame rate (60 -> 33/s); the title
now requests readback only for the surfaces it untiles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
